1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,813
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00:07,083 --> 00:00:07,916
ARCADE

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,083
BEFORE GERALD CHEN DISAPPEARED

4
00:00:11,166 --> 00:00:13,541
The professor's premise is a bit flawed.

5
00:00:13,625 --> 00:00:15,500
I organized those ideas into the report.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,166
How is it on your end?

7
00:00:24,208 --> 00:00:25,041
Okay.

8
00:00:25,125 --> 00:00:26,916
SPECIAL OFFER ON TOKENS, 404

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,041
I'll send it to you by 10:00 a.m. tomorrow.

10
00:00:29,125 --> 00:00:30,041
That's all for now.

11
00:01:12,916 --> 00:01:14,458
I left my laptop's power cord.

12
00:01:14,958 --> 00:01:16,458
I'm going back to campus.

13
00:01:30,666 --> 00:01:31,750
Don't move.

14
00:01:32,666 --> 00:01:34,375
Or I'll stab you.

15
00:01:35,291 --> 00:01:37,083
Stabbing from this angle?

16
00:01:37,166 --> 00:01:39,833
Even my grandma can do it. Why would we need you?

17
00:01:44,333 --> 00:01:46,541
Watch your back, not just what's ahead.

18
00:01:47,125 --> 00:01:48,666
You need more training.

19
00:01:50,041 --> 00:01:52,416
I only relaxed after hearing Ben's voice.

20
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:53,458
Let's try again.

21
00:01:53,541 --> 00:01:56,416
Again? I'll need to make a will first.

22
00:01:58,375 --> 00:02:00,708
Why did you make such a mess in here?

23
00:02:00,791 --> 00:02:03,791
Also, you disappeared for three to four months straight.

24
00:02:03,875 --> 00:02:04,958
Couldn't you reply?

25
00:02:07,166 --> 00:02:08,666
You still keep this on you?

26
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:11,208
Who says that?

27
00:02:11,291 --> 00:02:12,625
I just haven't tossed it.

28
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:14,833
Take it back.

29
00:02:20,208 --> 00:02:21,291
Mina…

30
00:02:23,375 --> 00:02:25,000
you were too careless just now.

31
00:02:25,625 --> 00:02:28,583
You must always have a plan B.

32
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:30,291
Got it?

33
00:02:32,708 --> 00:02:33,875
Got it.

34
00:02:37,375 --> 00:02:38,500
Also…

35
00:02:40,958 --> 00:02:41,875
Happy birthday.

36
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:51,250
Wishing you boundless health and good luck

37
00:02:51,333 --> 00:02:53,375
-Happy birthday -You know I don't celebrate.

38
00:02:53,458 --> 00:02:55,375
Stop singing. It's embarrassing.

39
00:02:55,458 --> 00:02:57,291
Then make a wish.

40
00:02:57,375 --> 00:02:59,375
I don't want to. Wishes are lies.

41
00:02:59,875 --> 00:03:01,083
You child.

42
00:03:01,166 --> 00:03:02,791
How are you so pessimistic?

43
00:03:02,875 --> 00:03:04,416
Come on, make a wish.

44
00:03:07,208 --> 00:03:08,208
Be good.

45
00:03:26,375 --> 00:03:28,291
THE FIXERS

46
00:03:45,958 --> 00:03:49,333
TIEN-BU-LA

47
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:55,333
Don't get in the car!

48
00:03:59,208 --> 00:04:00,166
Aren't you…

49
00:04:00,666 --> 00:04:02,208
Didn't you see

50
00:04:02,833 --> 00:04:03,875
how William died?

51
00:04:05,458 --> 00:04:07,166
You know so much about him.

52
00:04:08,291 --> 00:04:10,166
Do you think you can get away?

53
00:04:20,791 --> 00:04:22,750
Why are you looking into Zoe's death?

54
00:04:23,416 --> 00:04:26,083
Anyone connected to Zoe will end up like William.

55
00:04:26,583 --> 00:04:28,500
Do you believe he killed himself?

56
00:04:29,958 --> 00:04:31,041
I don't know.

57
00:04:31,625 --> 00:04:32,666
If you want to live,

58
00:04:33,250 --> 00:04:34,916
tell us everything you know.

59
00:04:36,416 --> 00:04:38,958
All I know is that Zoe left the company

60
00:04:39,458 --> 00:04:40,750
because she found out

61
00:04:40,833 --> 00:04:44,166
William secretly invested Yuan Tao's funds in Tolita for fraud.

62
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:47,208
Was her death related to William?

63
00:04:47,291 --> 00:04:49,250
When William found out, he panicked.

64
00:04:49,750 --> 00:04:51,166
He didn't seem to be acting.

65
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:55,958
Zoe's husband, Hsu Ming-yi, died a week before Zoe.

66
00:04:56,458 --> 00:04:57,541
You know that, right?

67
00:05:00,875 --> 00:05:03,583
The day Hsu Ming-yi died, he had called William.

68
00:05:03,666 --> 00:05:04,708
And?

69
00:05:05,291 --> 00:05:07,541
William seemed nervous when he answered the phone.

70
00:05:07,625 --> 00:05:08,625
I only heard him say,

71
00:05:09,916 --> 00:05:11,416
"Where did you hear that?"

72
00:05:12,333 --> 00:05:13,833
"They aren't to be messed with."

73
00:05:15,333 --> 00:05:17,625
But before he could finish, the call ended.

74
00:05:17,708 --> 00:05:18,958
I knew it.

75
00:05:19,041 --> 00:05:21,000
He learned something and was silenced.

76
00:05:21,083 --> 00:05:22,666
Have you ever seen this person?

77
00:05:26,625 --> 00:05:27,625
No.

78
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:34,625
After Zoe died,

79
00:05:34,708 --> 00:05:36,708
did William do anything strange?

80
00:05:43,208 --> 00:05:46,125
Hey, you had better think carefully.

81
00:05:46,208 --> 00:05:47,375
What haven't you told us?

82
00:05:51,083 --> 00:05:53,750
William did ask me to handle some dirty money.

83
00:05:53,833 --> 00:05:54,958
Why do you find that strange?

84
00:05:55,791 --> 00:05:58,583
He wanted me to store the money in a sound wallet.

85
00:05:58,666 --> 00:06:00,833
We never handled cash that way.

86
00:06:01,958 --> 00:06:03,583
A sound wallet?

87
00:06:04,083 --> 00:06:05,291
Who was it for?

88
00:06:05,375 --> 00:06:07,083
I don't know. He told me not to ask.

89
00:06:10,958 --> 00:06:12,875
That's really all I know.

90
00:06:15,791 --> 00:06:18,500
When you get to the airport, don't contact anyone.

91
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,333
Take the first flight out.

92
00:06:21,291 --> 00:06:22,375
Do you hear me?

93
00:06:27,208 --> 00:06:29,083
Could the person William said not to mess with

94
00:06:29,166 --> 00:06:31,125
and the owner of the sound wallet

95
00:06:32,125 --> 00:06:33,708
be the same person?

96
00:06:35,583 --> 00:06:38,291
Hey, what is this sound wallet thingy?

97
00:06:39,458 --> 00:06:42,708
Crypto users have 256-bit private keys,

98
00:06:43,208 --> 00:06:44,916
often managed with mnemonic phrases.

99
00:06:45,416 --> 00:06:47,250
But they can be easily lost on paper

100
00:06:47,333 --> 00:06:50,125
or stolen by hackers from computers.

101
00:06:50,625 --> 00:06:53,625
One way is to convert the password into a 30-second audio file.

102
00:06:53,708 --> 00:06:56,458
Decode it with software, and you can access the account.

103
00:06:56,541 --> 00:06:58,583
If we pursue this lead,

104
00:06:59,333 --> 00:07:01,666
we can trace the money and go from there.

105
00:07:02,166 --> 00:07:03,875
Seek and ye shall find,

106
00:07:03,958 --> 00:07:06,875
but beware of fake signs.

107
00:07:08,125 --> 00:07:10,166
But now William is dead,

108
00:07:10,250 --> 00:07:13,166
and we don't know where the sound wallet is.

109
00:07:13,250 --> 00:07:15,750
I say, why do the rich like to complicate things

110
00:07:15,833 --> 00:07:17,375
and use this weird wallet?

111
00:07:17,458 --> 00:07:20,416
Only cold cash you can see is safe.

112
00:07:20,916 --> 00:07:21,833
Right?

113
00:07:24,958 --> 00:07:26,083
Mina,

114
00:07:26,583 --> 00:07:28,625
did you say Gerald gave you your necklace?

115
00:07:40,958 --> 00:07:42,583
Why do you need this audio file?

116
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:45,000
It's better if you don't know.

117
00:07:45,958 --> 00:07:47,000
Not again.

118
00:07:47,083 --> 00:07:49,291
You still owe me a meal from last time.

119
00:07:52,541 --> 00:07:53,500
Hey, Taro!

120
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:54,875
Don't go there.

121
00:07:54,958 --> 00:07:56,416
You'll hit someone.

122
00:07:58,208 --> 00:07:59,166
Does he come here daily?

123
00:07:59,250 --> 00:08:01,708
Today is a holiday. The kindergarten is closed.

124
00:08:01,791 --> 00:08:04,375
He has to burn off energy. How else will he sleep?

125
00:08:04,458 --> 00:08:06,500
Can't you just buy him an iPad?

126
00:08:06,583 --> 00:08:08,250
Screen time can cause myopia, sir.

127
00:08:08,333 --> 00:08:10,500
Shall we take a break? I'll buy you ice cream.

128
00:08:10,583 --> 00:08:13,166
Ice cream has trans fats. You shouldn't eat it.

129
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:18,333
Hey, Gerald does have a crypto account.

130
00:08:30,375 --> 00:08:32,250
That's about 100 million NTD.

131
00:08:32,333 --> 00:08:33,625
One hundred million?

132
00:08:33,708 --> 00:08:34,875
Holy shit.

133
00:08:34,958 --> 00:08:36,583
He left you so much money?

134
00:08:37,083 --> 00:08:40,083
Gerald wouldn't just leave money.

135
00:08:40,583 --> 00:08:42,708
He must have left other clues.

136
00:08:47,916 --> 00:08:50,625
I traced Gerald's crypto account.

137
00:08:50,708 --> 00:08:53,375
There was a huge transfer just before he went missing.

138
00:08:53,458 --> 00:08:55,250
He bought a house in the mountains.

139
00:08:55,750 --> 00:08:57,708
I'll send you the address when I find it.

140
00:09:04,375 --> 00:09:06,041
Bought a house?

141
00:09:06,541 --> 00:09:08,625
Could he be hiding there?

142
00:09:14,666 --> 00:09:16,166
I'll go with you tomorrow.

143
00:09:17,625 --> 00:09:19,083
Who says I'm going?

144
00:09:20,166 --> 00:09:21,708
Maybe he is just

145
00:09:22,208 --> 00:09:24,375
trying not to get you involved.

146
00:09:27,958 --> 00:09:29,875
Gerald and Ben

147
00:09:30,458 --> 00:09:32,375
have always been protective of me.

148
00:09:34,833 --> 00:09:37,291
But they don't take good care of themselves.

149
00:09:39,541 --> 00:09:44,000
So you think he is still alive, right?

150
00:09:48,166 --> 00:09:49,958
We'll know when we find him tomorrow.

151
00:09:54,291 --> 00:09:55,333
Have some.

152
00:09:55,833 --> 00:09:56,833
It's getting cold.

153
00:10:00,583 --> 00:10:02,208
Why the radishes and meatballs?

154
00:10:02,708 --> 00:10:04,000
They aren't just for you.

155
00:10:04,541 --> 00:10:06,583
Why does anyone want to eat that?

156
00:10:06,666 --> 00:10:08,666
Do you want to try some deep-fried tofu?

157
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:09,916
No, the skin is gross.

158
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,708
You're so difficult. Try it.

159
00:10:11,791 --> 00:10:12,708
Fine, I'll eat it.

160
00:10:15,583 --> 00:10:16,916
That was a radish, wasn't it?

161
00:10:17,541 --> 00:10:18,958
-It's tofu. -Liar. Show me.

162
00:10:21,458 --> 00:10:22,708
-I didn't see it. -I ate it.

163
00:10:22,791 --> 00:10:23,791
No way. Have one more.

164
00:10:24,458 --> 00:10:26,750
-I just ate one. -You clearly ate a radish.

165
00:10:26,833 --> 00:10:27,750
Try some blood pudding.

166
00:10:27,833 --> 00:10:30,166
-You'll have a meatball after. -Try this.

167
00:10:32,208 --> 00:10:33,125
Have a pork…

168
00:10:34,250 --> 00:10:36,083
Okay, I'll have a pork meatball. Look.

169
00:10:39,125 --> 00:10:40,583
You clearly ate tofu.

170
00:10:45,291 --> 00:10:48,250
Why did Gerald leave Mina so much money?

171
00:10:48,333 --> 00:10:49,708
What is their relationship?

172
00:10:49,791 --> 00:10:50,791
AUTHENTIC TIEN-BU-LA

173
00:10:50,875 --> 00:10:52,041
Mina.

174
00:10:52,541 --> 00:10:54,750
She caught us finishing up a job.

175
00:10:54,833 --> 00:10:56,333
I was going to kill her.

176
00:10:56,833 --> 00:10:58,750
But Gerald saved her.

177
00:11:00,041 --> 00:11:01,708
So she's stuck around ever since?

178
00:11:01,791 --> 00:11:03,125
Doesn't she have family?

179
00:11:03,625 --> 00:11:05,625
She ran away from home.

180
00:11:06,125 --> 00:11:09,250
I never saw a child her age who was so--

181
00:11:09,333 --> 00:11:11,833
-Difficult. -Stubborn.

182
00:11:12,416 --> 00:11:13,583
St…

183
00:11:14,166 --> 00:11:16,666
Stubborn. She wasn't afraid of anything,

184
00:11:17,250 --> 00:11:20,208
as if she had seen the worst of it.

185
00:11:20,791 --> 00:11:23,083
So that's how she became who she is?

186
00:11:24,166 --> 00:11:25,208
Now I get it.

187
00:11:25,708 --> 00:11:26,583
Got it.

188
00:11:26,666 --> 00:11:30,708
But since meeting you guys, she has become more talkative.

189
00:11:30,791 --> 00:11:31,625
Has she?

190
00:11:34,333 --> 00:11:37,416
So you believe Gerald isn't dead?

191
00:11:39,583 --> 00:11:40,833
In our line of work,

192
00:11:41,333 --> 00:11:43,500
how many of us actually make it to retirement?

193
00:11:44,083 --> 00:11:45,416
If I hadn't lost this leg,

194
00:11:46,208 --> 00:11:48,291
I might have died long ago.

195
00:11:48,875 --> 00:11:50,375
What happened to your leg?

196
00:11:52,166 --> 00:11:53,958
A failed mission.

197
00:11:54,458 --> 00:11:56,916
Yeh Yueh Tong saw me as useless,

198
00:11:57,416 --> 00:11:59,041
so they let me go.

199
00:11:59,125 --> 00:12:00,458
So cruel?

200
00:12:00,541 --> 00:12:02,083
Fucking hell.

201
00:12:03,250 --> 00:12:05,125
Hey, here's what.

202
00:12:05,208 --> 00:12:08,208
When I retire, I'll open a stall like you.

203
00:12:08,291 --> 00:12:10,625
I'll sell swamp eel noodles right next to you.

204
00:12:10,708 --> 00:12:12,958
A one-stop shop. It'll profit. Sound good?

205
00:12:13,041 --> 00:12:15,416
Leave me out of it. I don't like crowds.

206
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:17,208
If you do open a stall, stay away.

207
00:12:17,291 --> 00:12:19,250
Aren't you glad I'm keeping you company?

208
00:12:19,333 --> 00:12:22,208
I'm worried you will feel lonely and cold.

209
00:12:27,291 --> 00:12:29,000
You don't get it.

210
00:12:29,083 --> 00:12:29,958
Have your soup.

211
00:12:30,041 --> 00:12:31,125
I had enough.

212
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:32,541
-Have some tofu. -Enough.

213
00:12:32,625 --> 00:12:34,000
I'm home.

214
00:12:34,083 --> 00:12:35,500
You're back?

215
00:12:35,583 --> 00:12:37,458
You're still awake? Perfect. Here.

216
00:12:37,958 --> 00:12:39,000
Where is Howie?

217
00:12:39,083 --> 00:12:40,041
Studying in his room.

218
00:12:40,666 --> 00:12:43,875
I got you a snack, tien-bu-la. There's blood pudding, your favorite.

219
00:12:44,833 --> 00:12:46,208
Howie,

220
00:12:46,291 --> 00:12:49,583
your dad bought you a late-night snack. Come over and eat.

221
00:12:50,625 --> 00:12:51,833
Hey, hold on.

222
00:12:53,541 --> 00:12:55,333
What is in that bag?

223
00:12:58,583 --> 00:13:01,291
Goldie said I needed more clothes and bought me some.

224
00:13:02,291 --> 00:13:03,958
Your boss treats you really well.

225
00:13:04,458 --> 00:13:05,666
So handsome and generous.

226
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:07,750
Invite him over for dinner more often.

227
00:13:07,833 --> 00:13:09,583
Sure.

228
00:13:24,125 --> 00:13:26,291
What's going on? Why are you hiding in your room?

229
00:13:27,041 --> 00:13:28,541
I'm about to take a shower.

230
00:13:29,208 --> 00:13:31,916
-You act all sneaky. What are you up to? -Come on.

231
00:13:33,833 --> 00:13:35,250
Seriously.

232
00:14:04,083 --> 00:14:05,250
You look happy.

233
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:08,541
Do you remember what your dad got me for my last birthday?

234
00:14:08,625 --> 00:14:10,791
That. A fill light for live streaming.

235
00:14:10,875 --> 00:14:12,916
Yes. And he added, well,

236
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,666
"With the light done right,

237
00:14:14,750 --> 00:14:16,375
Wendy glows so fairylike."

238
00:14:16,458 --> 00:14:17,500
It sucked.

239
00:14:17,583 --> 00:14:19,125
He's like that every time.

240
00:14:19,208 --> 00:14:20,583
Let me tell you.

241
00:14:21,083 --> 00:14:22,125
Your dad

242
00:14:22,833 --> 00:14:24,750
finally figured it out this year.

243
00:14:28,958 --> 00:14:29,791
Madam Fan.

244
00:14:31,166 --> 00:14:32,875
They found Gerald.

245
00:14:36,416 --> 00:14:38,000
Don't alert them.

246
00:14:38,833 --> 00:14:41,208
Send a fixer to keep an eye on them.

247
00:14:41,916 --> 00:14:44,500
If anything happens, report back.

248
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,083
Okay.

249
00:14:46,791 --> 00:14:48,416
As long as he's alive,

250
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:50,666
we can't give our client an answer.

251
00:14:51,166 --> 00:14:52,375
You know what to do.

252
00:14:54,541 --> 00:14:56,666
No loose ends.

253
00:14:57,541 --> 00:15:00,041
Yeh Yueh Tong doesn't need any more trouble.

254
00:15:00,541 --> 00:15:01,416
Okay.

255
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:19,833
-Where are you? -I've got things to do at home.

256
00:15:19,916 --> 00:15:22,000
I won't be joining you to be the third wheel today.

257
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,166
Trying to slack off?

258
00:15:24,250 --> 00:15:26,375
The crisp autumn air is perfect for an outing.

259
00:15:26,458 --> 00:15:28,791
Seize your chance, okay? Bye.

260
00:15:28,875 --> 00:15:29,708
Hey.

261
00:15:53,083 --> 00:15:56,041
When you get to the US, if you need money, just ask.

262
00:15:56,125 --> 00:15:58,833
I heard that things are crazy expensive there.

263
00:15:58,916 --> 00:16:00,250
Don't struggle out of pride.

264
00:16:00,333 --> 00:16:02,750
Don't worry. You gave me more than enough to spend.

265
00:16:02,833 --> 00:16:04,541
And I applied for an on-campus job.

266
00:16:04,625 --> 00:16:05,916
I'll make sure to repay you.

267
00:16:06,416 --> 00:16:08,791
This is what I owed your dad anyway.

268
00:16:08,875 --> 00:16:10,041
Felix,

269
00:16:10,125 --> 00:16:11,333
you've got it wrong.

270
00:16:11,958 --> 00:16:14,000
You've been taking care of me all these years.

271
00:16:14,083 --> 00:16:15,958
You paid for it all when my mom was sick.

272
00:16:16,041 --> 00:16:17,375
We owe you.

273
00:16:19,875 --> 00:16:22,333
Stop worrying about money. Your studies matter most.

274
00:16:22,416 --> 00:16:24,750
I'll take you to the airport tomorrow morning.

275
00:16:24,833 --> 00:16:27,125
No need. I've booked a ride.

276
00:16:33,083 --> 00:16:35,666
This is for you, on behalf of your dad.

277
00:16:37,416 --> 00:16:39,250
Your dad's greatest wish was

278
00:16:39,333 --> 00:16:41,750
to send you abroad to study

279
00:16:41,833 --> 00:16:43,416
and see the world for him.

280
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:44,666
Now you're fulfilling it.

281
00:16:47,041 --> 00:16:47,916
Put it on for me.

282
00:16:48,791 --> 00:16:50,000
Okay, come on.

283
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,500
From now on,

284
00:16:53,583 --> 00:16:56,500
whenever you wear it,

285
00:16:57,125 --> 00:16:58,250
it will feel like…

286
00:16:58,791 --> 00:17:01,333
It will feel like your dad is with you.

287
00:17:04,666 --> 00:17:06,166
Okay, done.

288
00:17:08,666 --> 00:17:10,291
I will come visit you.

289
00:17:11,583 --> 00:17:13,000
Take good care of yourself.

290
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:21,708
Don't cry, or you'll look uglier than your dad.

291
00:17:22,250 --> 00:17:25,083
Why are you always like this at these moments?

292
00:17:25,166 --> 00:17:26,166
You're annoying.

293
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:27,875
I… I'm going to pee.

294
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,500
Weirdo.

295
00:17:41,416 --> 00:17:43,250
Why are you stepping down so suddenly?

296
00:17:43,916 --> 00:17:47,083
Do you have a successor in mind?

297
00:17:50,791 --> 00:17:52,333
I'm old and useless.

298
00:17:52,416 --> 00:17:54,041
It's time to step down, so I will.

299
00:17:54,541 --> 00:17:56,375
The exit is still here.

300
00:17:57,125 --> 00:17:58,833
It's easy to back out.

301
00:17:58,916 --> 00:18:01,000
By the time it is removed,

302
00:18:01,541 --> 00:18:04,500
you will be battered no matter how you leave.

303
00:18:05,916 --> 00:18:07,000
Fixer Terra,

304
00:18:08,375 --> 00:18:10,125
that door is heavy.

305
00:18:11,416 --> 00:18:13,083
It will take many people

306
00:18:13,583 --> 00:18:14,875
to remove it.

307
00:18:15,583 --> 00:18:17,583
Indeed, many people want to do that.

308
00:18:20,166 --> 00:18:22,375
Like father, like daughter.

309
00:18:24,083 --> 00:18:26,333
Those who support her, an outsider,

310
00:18:26,916 --> 00:18:30,208
outnumber those who support you, an insider.

311
00:18:33,041 --> 00:18:35,333
I'm old, so I won't meddle anymore.

312
00:18:43,166 --> 00:18:44,541
Old friend,

313
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:48,458
I hope you can leave on a high note.

314
00:18:48,958 --> 00:18:50,666
I'll be waiting to have tea with you.

315
00:18:59,250 --> 00:19:02,875
THE TIMES ARE AGAINST ME. WHAT CAN I DO?

316
00:19:04,833 --> 00:19:05,875
Excuse me.

317
00:19:06,375 --> 00:19:08,250
Could you interpret this fortune slip?

318
00:19:11,958 --> 00:19:14,708
"Your path to fame is not yet clear."

319
00:19:15,208 --> 00:19:17,958
"With stormy clashes drawing near."

320
00:19:18,833 --> 00:19:22,333
"Guard both sides from loss and pain."

321
00:19:23,208 --> 00:19:26,833
"Step back, sigh not, and wait again."

322
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:31,541
Are you asking about your family or career?

323
00:19:32,125 --> 00:19:33,708
Madam Fan got this for you.

324
00:19:54,750 --> 00:19:55,583
Hello?

325
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:12,083
Go up this path, and we'll be there.

326
00:20:12,166 --> 00:20:14,208
LIEN HSIN BRIDGE

327
00:21:15,375 --> 00:21:17,125
His goal is probably the same as ours.

328
00:21:17,208 --> 00:21:18,791
He's a fixer at Yeh Yueh Tong.

329
00:21:19,291 --> 00:21:21,416
Madam Fan knows we've found Gerald.

330
00:21:23,625 --> 00:21:24,500
Let's go.

331
00:22:05,416 --> 00:22:06,250
Excuse me.

332
00:22:07,458 --> 00:22:09,291
Have you seen this person?

333
00:22:12,208 --> 00:22:13,041
Thank you.

334
00:22:20,791 --> 00:22:24,458
All branches have been notified of the time of the secret meeting.

335
00:22:27,708 --> 00:22:29,250
God just offered guidance.

336
00:22:29,333 --> 00:22:31,125
I drew stick number 28.

337
00:22:31,625 --> 00:22:34,083
"The golden days of old have nearly gone."

338
00:22:34,583 --> 00:22:36,833
"A tiger once mighty, now stranded and drawn."

339
00:22:36,916 --> 00:22:38,708
"Fortune is fickle, fey, and fleet."

340
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:42,000
"So seize the hour before it flees."

341
00:22:44,666 --> 00:22:46,875
Do you remember the stories behind this verse?

342
00:22:47,375 --> 00:22:52,625
One is Cao Cao's capture by Zhang Xiu in Wancheng.

343
00:22:53,416 --> 00:22:55,875
The other is Xiang Yu's defeat.

344
00:22:55,958 --> 00:22:59,958
Surrounded by enemies, he slit his own throat at the Wu River.

345
00:23:01,625 --> 00:23:03,125
One was betrayed,

346
00:23:03,625 --> 00:23:05,708
but ultimately managed to escape danger

347
00:23:05,791 --> 00:23:07,166
and fulfill his ambition.

348
00:23:08,291 --> 00:23:10,583
The other was a dispirited hero

349
00:23:11,208 --> 00:23:13,125
who reached the end of the line.

350
00:23:15,583 --> 00:23:16,458
In your opinion,

351
00:23:17,333 --> 00:23:18,500
which one

352
00:23:18,583 --> 00:23:20,375
is the fortune slip referring to?

353
00:23:21,125 --> 00:23:22,375
This depends on

354
00:23:22,875 --> 00:23:25,458
whether the person can adapt to the situation

355
00:23:25,541 --> 00:23:27,375
and swallow his pride to survive.

356
00:23:31,625 --> 00:23:32,750
You're right.

357
00:23:34,375 --> 00:23:36,583
Is there anything else you need me for?

358
00:23:37,333 --> 00:23:38,166
No.

359
00:23:38,833 --> 00:23:41,458
You have worked hard for Ching He lately.

360
00:23:41,541 --> 00:23:43,083
Take a few days off to rest.

361
00:23:50,208 --> 00:23:52,916
You asked Fixer Gold to help find Gerald.

362
00:23:53,583 --> 00:23:55,291
Aren't you afraid of the fallout

363
00:23:55,375 --> 00:23:57,250
when he learns the truth?

364
00:24:00,916 --> 00:24:02,416
If it's something he must know,

365
00:24:02,916 --> 00:24:05,000
someone is bound to tell him.

366
00:24:06,875 --> 00:24:10,208
I only fear that this move was too hasty.

367
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:13,333
Certain things, once known,

368
00:24:13,916 --> 00:24:15,458
cannot be unknown.

369
00:24:28,041 --> 00:24:30,750
Someone looks after the potted plants out front.

370
00:24:32,041 --> 00:24:33,708
We should be able to catch them.

371
00:25:07,791 --> 00:25:09,000
Zoe.

372
00:25:14,541 --> 00:25:15,458
Who are you guys?

373
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:17,500
Stay back.

374
00:25:18,250 --> 00:25:19,666
Put the gun down.

375
00:25:20,166 --> 00:25:21,375
Don't hurt the child.

376
00:25:21,458 --> 00:25:22,291
Back off!

377
00:25:27,750 --> 00:25:28,666
You guys…

378
00:25:29,500 --> 00:25:31,208
Why won't you let me go?

379
00:25:31,291 --> 00:25:33,083
We won't hurt you.

380
00:25:33,166 --> 00:25:34,541
I'm here for Gerald Chen.

381
00:25:39,166 --> 00:25:40,625
He disappeared over a year ago.

382
00:25:40,708 --> 00:25:42,416
He left me clues

383
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:43,958
to find this place.

384
00:25:53,625 --> 00:25:55,041
You're the one in the photo.

385
00:26:29,500 --> 00:26:31,125
What is your relationship

386
00:26:31,708 --> 00:26:33,250
with Gerald?

387
00:26:41,250 --> 00:26:43,000
He came to kill me.

388
00:26:52,750 --> 00:26:53,750
Are you here?

389
00:26:54,250 --> 00:26:55,458
I'm not coming.

390
00:26:56,333 --> 00:26:57,541
Don't contact me again.

391
00:26:57,625 --> 00:26:59,083
Hello? William.

392
00:26:59,583 --> 00:27:00,541
Hello?

393
00:27:19,666 --> 00:27:23,333
But he couldn't make himself do it when he saw that I was pregnant.

394
00:27:26,916 --> 00:27:28,541
Gerald didn't complete his mission.

395
00:27:29,125 --> 00:27:32,541
Yeh Yueh Tong wouldn't have spared him, and you shouldn't still be here.

396
00:27:33,875 --> 00:27:35,708
That's why he faked my death.

397
00:27:47,583 --> 00:27:49,125
We fooled everyone.

398
00:27:51,958 --> 00:27:53,041
Target Zoe

399
00:27:53,541 --> 00:27:54,666
confirmed dead.

400
00:27:58,333 --> 00:28:00,041
Why are you helping me so much?

401
00:28:00,875 --> 00:28:02,125
I don't want to mess up again.

402
00:28:05,416 --> 00:28:07,041
He put me here to lie low.

403
00:28:08,250 --> 00:28:09,541
So where is he?

404
00:28:10,791 --> 00:28:13,291
GERALD CHEN

405
00:28:15,500 --> 00:28:17,541
-Hello? -I don't think I can make it.

406
00:28:18,041 --> 00:28:20,083
There's a bag of cash in the ceiling.

407
00:28:20,166 --> 00:28:22,291
It should be enough for you and your daughter.

408
00:28:22,375 --> 00:28:23,791
Once things calm down, I--

409
00:28:25,125 --> 00:28:25,958
Hello?

410
00:28:27,125 --> 00:28:27,958
Hello?

411
00:28:30,291 --> 00:28:31,125
Hello?

412
00:28:32,166 --> 00:28:35,041
I haven't heard from him since that day.

413
00:28:40,375 --> 00:28:41,583
He might be dead.

414
00:28:41,666 --> 00:28:42,833
Impossible.

415
00:28:42,916 --> 00:28:45,333
He must have planned everything beforehand.

416
00:28:46,208 --> 00:28:47,916
When he was sent to kill me,

417
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:50,000
he already knew he might die.

418
00:28:52,625 --> 00:28:53,833
What do you mean?

419
00:28:57,666 --> 00:29:00,041
Before his mission, Gerald must have expected

420
00:29:00,125 --> 00:29:03,583
that Yeh Yueh Tong would eliminate him to keep it a secret.

421
00:29:13,208 --> 00:29:15,041
Why did Yeh Yueh Tong want to kill you?

422
00:29:16,625 --> 00:29:19,375
What is this secret that so many people had to die for?

423
00:29:26,375 --> 00:29:27,541
It's you, the Hsuehs.

424
00:29:28,416 --> 00:29:29,625
What do you mean?

425
00:29:30,208 --> 00:29:31,625
The Hsueh family

426
00:29:32,958 --> 00:29:33,916
killed my husband

427
00:29:34,875 --> 00:29:36,500
and came after my daughter and me.

428
00:29:37,500 --> 00:29:39,041
If it weren't for my daughter,

429
00:29:39,541 --> 00:29:41,541
I would have taken you all down with me.

430
00:29:41,625 --> 00:29:43,375
-Why do the Hsuehs-- -Stay back!

431
00:29:52,166 --> 00:29:54,166
Anyhow, a life for a life.

432
00:29:54,250 --> 00:29:55,833
It's only fair.

433
00:29:56,416 --> 00:29:57,500
Calm down.

434
00:29:58,166 --> 00:30:00,708
I just want to know why the Hsuehs want to kill William

435
00:30:01,291 --> 00:30:02,458
and your husband.

436
00:30:05,500 --> 00:30:07,708
Do you really not know, or are you playing dumb?

437
00:30:08,708 --> 00:30:11,916
The Hsin Nan redevelopment project was massive, but approved quickly.

438
00:30:12,500 --> 00:30:14,375
You think the Hsuehs had no hand in it?

439
00:30:15,583 --> 00:30:17,875
William laundered a huge sum of money for them.

440
00:30:17,958 --> 00:30:19,333
How could you not have known?

441
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:36,916
I just want my daughter and me to be safe.

442
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:38,666
Just pretend that I'm dead.

443
00:30:39,375 --> 00:30:40,916
I won't say anything.

444
00:30:42,916 --> 00:30:44,000
Don't worry.

445
00:30:44,666 --> 00:30:46,333
We won't tell anyone.

446
00:30:55,875 --> 00:30:57,958
Happy birthday to you

447
00:30:58,541 --> 00:31:00,458
Happy birthday to you

448
00:31:01,041 --> 00:31:03,166
Happy birthday to you

449
00:31:03,250 --> 00:31:05,500
Happy birthday to you

450
00:31:05,583 --> 00:31:07,583
Okay, blow out the candles. Come on.

451
00:31:09,416 --> 00:31:11,958
Mom, happy birthday.

452
00:31:13,041 --> 00:31:14,666
My good son!

453
00:31:14,750 --> 00:31:16,083
Thank you.

454
00:31:16,166 --> 00:31:18,333
You have a good husband too, okay?

455
00:31:19,458 --> 00:31:20,458
Thank you.

456
00:31:20,541 --> 00:31:21,750
MOM

457
00:31:22,541 --> 00:31:23,416
Perfume?

458
00:31:23,500 --> 00:31:25,500
Yes. Hey, do you remember?

459
00:31:25,583 --> 00:31:28,833
We went shopping at a mall when you were pregnant with Howie.

460
00:31:28,916 --> 00:31:31,375
You saw this perfume and really liked it,

461
00:31:31,458 --> 00:31:33,125
but didn't want to splurge on it.

462
00:31:33,208 --> 00:31:34,208
Here, look.

463
00:31:41,500 --> 00:31:42,500
Felix.

464
00:31:43,375 --> 00:31:45,291
There are no secrets in marriage, right?

465
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:49,875
Are you hiding something from me?

466
00:31:51,250 --> 00:31:53,625
What could I be hiding from you?

467
00:31:54,458 --> 00:31:57,291
Stop imagining things. Go to sleep, okay? Come on.

468
00:31:57,791 --> 00:31:59,000
Are you sure?

469
00:31:59,916 --> 00:32:01,250
I'm sure!

470
00:32:03,333 --> 00:32:05,291
You're being weird.

471
00:32:13,041 --> 00:32:15,333
The brat didn't tell her, did he?

472
00:32:16,375 --> 00:32:17,291
What did you say?

473
00:32:18,166 --> 00:32:19,791
Nothing.

474
00:32:20,291 --> 00:32:22,166
Just sleep. Stop overthinking.

475
00:32:22,666 --> 00:32:24,500
Be good. Go to sleep. Come on.

476
00:32:30,416 --> 00:32:32,125
Based on the exam results,

477
00:32:33,666 --> 00:32:36,291
Mr. Hsueh's liver cancer has metastasized.

478
00:32:36,791 --> 00:32:39,000
We need to start treatment as soon as possible.

479
00:32:41,958 --> 00:32:43,083
Okay, I understand.

480
00:32:43,666 --> 00:32:44,625
Doctor,

481
00:32:44,708 --> 00:32:47,291
this must remain confidential.

482
00:32:47,375 --> 00:32:48,291
Okay.

483
00:32:54,916 --> 00:32:56,416
My illness

484
00:32:56,916 --> 00:32:58,750
might be helpful to you.

485
00:33:00,083 --> 00:33:01,750
Announce it to the public

486
00:33:02,541 --> 00:33:03,833
at the right time.

487
00:33:05,208 --> 00:33:07,125
We're at a critical moment.

488
00:33:08,583 --> 00:33:09,916
There's no room for error.

489
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:11,041
Got it?

490
00:33:17,125 --> 00:33:18,083
Also,

491
00:33:19,458 --> 00:33:21,208
don't tell your brother yet.

492
00:33:23,791 --> 00:33:24,625
Okay.

493
00:33:27,458 --> 00:33:28,291
Dad,

494
00:33:28,958 --> 00:33:30,583
get some rest.

495
00:33:49,375 --> 00:33:50,583
Things have changed.

496
00:33:55,791 --> 00:33:57,083
I always thought that

497
00:33:57,583 --> 00:33:59,625
as long as Ben and I kept searching…

498
00:34:01,750 --> 00:34:03,250
that meant he was still alive.

499
00:34:09,083 --> 00:34:11,000
He left you the necklace.

500
00:34:11,958 --> 00:34:16,041
Maybe he had hoped that one day you'd see him in that house.

501
00:34:19,250 --> 00:34:21,583
He knew he was going to die.

502
00:34:21,666 --> 00:34:23,791
That's why he left me the necklace

503
00:34:24,333 --> 00:34:25,875
before going on his mission.

504
00:34:26,916 --> 00:34:29,458
It's just that he never thought you'd join Yeh Yueh Tong.

505
00:34:31,083 --> 00:34:32,541
What will you do now?

506
00:34:33,541 --> 00:34:35,875
Madam Fan has kept me around for so long

507
00:34:36,416 --> 00:34:38,458
just to find out Gerald's whereabouts.

508
00:34:47,875 --> 00:34:48,708
What?

509
00:34:52,208 --> 00:34:53,958
Zoe is still alive.

510
00:34:54,500 --> 00:34:56,458
This isn't just bad for Yeh Yueh Tong.

511
00:34:58,166 --> 00:34:59,541
It's also a threat

512
00:35:00,500 --> 00:35:01,875
to the Hsueh family.

513
00:35:01,958 --> 00:35:03,000
I won't harm her.

514
00:35:03,083 --> 00:35:04,625
I know you won't.

515
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:08,208
At least not now.

516
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:09,875
What do you mean?

517
00:35:11,541 --> 00:35:13,416
Who knows if you will bring Zoe home

518
00:35:14,208 --> 00:35:15,416
to score points?

519
00:35:18,958 --> 00:35:21,166
You've been using me to find Zoe from the start.

520
00:35:21,791 --> 00:35:22,625
Right?

521
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:31,333
Ching He is having a secret meeting today.

522
00:35:31,416 --> 00:35:34,083
All six chairpersons will attend.

523
00:35:36,083 --> 00:35:39,041
I'm sure it will be a good show.

524
00:35:46,166 --> 00:35:47,875
TERRA

525
00:35:47,958 --> 00:35:51,083
Fixer Terra isn't one to be late.

526
00:35:51,583 --> 00:35:52,708
What is going on today?

527
00:35:52,791 --> 00:35:54,166
EARTH

528
00:35:56,291 --> 00:35:57,125
Oh.

529
00:35:57,666 --> 00:35:58,500
Wait.

530
00:35:59,500 --> 00:36:01,291
One will be missing.

531
00:36:04,666 --> 00:36:05,500
Folks.

532
00:36:08,875 --> 00:36:09,791
Chairman.

533
00:36:10,750 --> 00:36:12,708
Fixer Terra is not coming.

534
00:36:14,250 --> 00:36:16,500
He was found

535
00:36:16,583 --> 00:36:18,333
dead in the suburbs.

536
00:36:22,125 --> 00:36:23,625
How could this be?

537
00:36:24,875 --> 00:36:27,916
We will pause our discussion for today

538
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:32,333
until I figure out what happened to Fixer Terra.

539
00:36:33,791 --> 00:36:34,875
Chairman,

540
00:36:35,958 --> 00:36:39,333
we should carefully discuss

541
00:36:39,916 --> 00:36:41,750
whether there are better candidates

542
00:36:42,375 --> 00:36:44,791
for the position of Fixer Celestial.

543
00:36:47,833 --> 00:36:49,250
What do you mean by that?

544
00:36:50,250 --> 00:36:54,708
The Hong family has served Ching He for generations.

545
00:36:56,041 --> 00:36:57,333
Everything we do

546
00:36:58,000 --> 00:37:00,083
is in Ching He's best interests.

547
00:37:01,625 --> 00:37:03,833
It has stood strong for over a century

548
00:37:04,333 --> 00:37:05,166
thanks to

549
00:37:05,666 --> 00:37:08,708
leaders who adapted to change

550
00:37:08,791 --> 00:37:11,208
and made the right choices.

551
00:37:12,708 --> 00:37:14,375
Sir Hong has agreed

552
00:37:14,458 --> 00:37:17,000
to hand over the key to the Kuang Ming Chamber.

553
00:37:17,500 --> 00:37:21,625
But Thackery won't step down so easily.

554
00:37:28,583 --> 00:37:30,416
After an incident this serious,

555
00:37:30,500 --> 00:37:32,166
as chairman,

556
00:37:32,666 --> 00:37:37,125
it is my ultimate responsibility to find out why.

557
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:48,416
I have a way to deal with Thackery.

558
00:37:48,500 --> 00:37:49,708
Please do tell.

559
00:37:50,208 --> 00:37:51,916
You will know when the time comes.

560
00:37:53,583 --> 00:37:54,416
Madam Fan,

561
00:37:55,250 --> 00:37:56,416
to our great partnership.

562
00:38:52,333 --> 00:38:53,375
LULLABY

563
00:39:19,208 --> 00:39:20,458
This will save your life.

564
00:39:20,541 --> 00:39:22,791
If you're ever in danger,

565
00:39:22,875 --> 00:39:24,458
use this to contact Ching He.

566
00:39:24,541 --> 00:39:27,666
CHING HE TEMPLE

567
00:40:19,500 --> 00:40:20,333
Hello?

568
00:40:21,333 --> 00:40:22,250
Hello?

569
00:40:22,750 --> 00:40:24,083
Gerald Chen said

570
00:40:24,750 --> 00:40:26,416
